  <data name="Efi_What_Settings" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stage 2: SIP, the boot-args and the quirks.</value></data>
  <data name="Efi_What_Safari" xml:space="preserve"><value>The Safari setting: Apple Secure Boot off, for the system-volume copy of the Metal driver.</value></data>
  <data name="Efi_What_SettingsSafari" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stage 2 and the Safari setting as one change: one backup, one restart.</value></data>
  <data name="Efi_What_Driver" xml:space="preserve"><value>Stage 4: IntelXe.kext and its config.plist entry (SSDT-ARCOFF.aml when its path is confirmed, HybridPM.kext on a hybrid CPU).</value></data>
  <data name="Efi_What_Undo" xml:space="preserve"><value>From the newest backup not yet put back: the files the last change touched.</value></data>
  <data name="Efi_Plan_Safety" xml:space="preserve"><value>Backs up the whole EFI folder first, then makes exactly these changes. If the EFI changed since this list was made, nothing is written. Restart afterwards.</value></data>
  <data name="Efi_Undo_Safety" xml:space="preserve"><value>Puts back, from the last backup, the files that change replaced. The backup stays. Restart afterwards.</value></data>
